###  1. Summary of the impact \(indicative maximum 100 words\) 

 Our work has directly changed the first\-line treatment for women with non\-atypical endometrial hyperplasia \(EH\). Previously, this was operative hysterectomy whereas our work has shown excellent outcomes with the use of a progestogen\-releasing coil \(LNG\-IUS\) inserted into the womb. 

 As a result we have: 

1.  **Improved patient health and well\-being**, as fewer women now suffer fertility loss and the complications associated with hysterectomy, whilst benefiting from reduced risk of endometrial cancer; 

1.  **Changed UK and international guidelines** for the management of EH; 

1.  **Changed clinical practice in EH** management by >90% of UK gynaecologists.

